# Studio Booking: Odoo UI Rules

## Visual Goals

- Professional, clean, premium-looking backend UI
- Strong grouping and visual hierarchy
- Mobile-aware where possible; optimized for operators
- Restrained use of decorations and badges

---

## Form Layout

- Use `<group string="...">` for logical sections (General, Assignment, Schedule, Recurring)
- Two-column groups where appropriate
- Hide tenant_id for tenant users: `invisible="1"` with `groups="studio_booking.group_studio_booking_user"`
- Show tenant_id for managers: `groups="studio_booking.group_studio_booking_manager"`
- Use `readonly="1"` for computed/audit fields (booking_status, waitlist_sequence, booked_by_user_id)

---

## List Views

- Readable columns; avoid clutter
- Use `decoration-muted` for inactive/archived (e.g. `decoration-muted="not active"`)
- Header buttons for bulk actions (e.g. Cancel Booking(s))
- Domain on relational fields to restrict choices (e.g. session_id: `state not in ['cancelled','completed']`)

---

## Search Views

- Practical filters and group-by options
- Meaningful default filters where helpful

---

## Calendar Views

- Use for `studio.class_session` (session_start, session_end)
- Include capacity, booked_count, waitlist_count, booked_display, waitlist_display
- Color by instructor_id or similar for visual distinction

---

## Notebook Pages

- Use only when useful (e.g. Bookings tab, Generated Sessions tab)
- Keep pages focused; avoid excessive nesting

---

## Header Buttons

- Statusbar for lifecycle models: `statusbar_visible="scheduled,cancelled,completed"`
- Action buttons: Detail (action_booking_detail), Cancel Session (action_cancel_session)
- Use `invisible` for state-dependent visibility (e.g. Cancel invisible when state=='cancelled')

---

## Smart Buttons

- Use when helpful for quick navigation (e.g. count of related records)
- Avoid clutter; one or two per form when they add value

---

## Role-Aware Visibility

- `groups="studio_booking.group_studio_booking_manager"` for tenant_id, cross-tenant actions
- `invisible="not is_recurring"` for recurring-specific fields
- `required="is_recurring and recurring_range == 'week'"` for conditional required

---

## SCSS Usage

- Targeted enhancements only (e.g. branch_list column widths)
- Use module-specific class (e.g. `o_studio_branch_list`) to avoid global pollution
- No visual chaos; keep changes minimal and purposeful
